<config xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:module:Magento_Config:etc/system_file.xsd">
    <system>
        <tab id="yireo" sortOrder="999" translate="label">
            <label>Yireo</label>
        </tab>
        <section id="googletagmanager2" translate="label" sortOrder="342" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
            <label>Yireo GoogleTagManager</label>
            <tab>yireo</tab>
            <resource>Yireo_GoogleTagManager2::config</resource>
            <group id="settings" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="1" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                <label>Settings</label>
                <field id="funding" type="note" sortOrder="1" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Funding</label>
                    <frontend_model>Yireo\GoogleTagManager2\Config\Frontend\Funding</frontend_model>
                </field>
                <field id="enabled" type="select" translate="label" sortOrder="1" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Enabled</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                </field>
                <field id="id" translate="label" sortOrder="2" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Container Public ID</label>
                    <comment>ID of your Google Tag container, starting with "GTM-"</comment>
                    <frontend_model>Yireo\GoogleTagManager2\Config\Frontend\ContainerId</frontend_model>
                    <backend_model>Yireo\GoogleTagManager2\Config\Backend\ContainerId</backend_model>
                    <validate>validate-ga4-container-id</validate>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="environment_auth" translate="label comment" sortOrder="3" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>GTM Environment Auth</label>
                    <comment><![CDATA[Value of <code>gtm_auth</code> in the snippet under <b>GTM &gt; Admin &gt; Environments &gt; Get Snippet</b>. Only applied to the first container ID. <b>Warning</b>: Only set this for development or staging (preferably via <code>bin/magento config:set --lock-env</code>), so that it never ends up in production.]]></comment>
                    <backend_model>Yireo\GoogleTagManager2\Config\Backend\EnvironmentAuth</backend_model>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="environment_preview" translate="label comment" sortOrder="3" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>GTM Environment Preview</label>
                    <comment><![CDATA[Value of <code>gtm_preview</code> (like <code>env-6</code>). Both this value and the GTM Environment Auth need to be set.]]></comment>
                    <backend_model>Yireo\GoogleTagManager2\Config\Backend\EnvironmentPreview</backend_model>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="debug" type="select" translate="label" sortOrder="4" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Debug</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="debug_clicks" type="select" translate="label" sortOrder="4" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Debug Clicks</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="debug">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="wait_for_ui" type="select" translate="label" sortOrder="4" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Wait for user interaction</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="load_container" type="select" translate="label comment" sortOrder="6" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Load GTM container script</label>
                    <comment>When set to No, the extension still pushes the gtm.js start event and all dataLayer events, but no longer inserts the gtm.js script itself. Use this when the container is already loaded by something else, for instance a first-party Google tag gateway (like the one of Cloudflare) that injects its own loader. That loader should not push the gtm.js event itself and should run after the consent defaults. See the README for details.</comment>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="category_products" translate="label" sortOrder="5" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Maximum Products in Category</label>
                    <comment>Maximum number of products to load in a specific category overview. 0 to disable</comment>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="product_list_value_on_category" type="select" translate="label" sortOrder="5" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Product List Value on Category Page</label>
                    <source_model>Yireo\GoogleTagManager2\Config\Source\ProductListValue</source_model>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="product_eav_attributes" type="multiselect" translate="label" sortOrder="5" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Product EAV Attributes</label>
                    <source_model>Yireo\GoogleTagManager2\Config\Source\ProductAttributes</source_model>
                    <comment>Product EAV attributes to show in datalayer</comment>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="category_eav_attributes" type="multiselect" translate="label" sortOrder="5" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Category EAV Attributes</label>
                    <source_model>Yireo\GoogleTagManager2\Config\Source\CategoryAttributes</source_model>
                    <comment>Category EAV attributes to show in datalayer</comment>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="customer_eav_attributes" type="multiselect" translate="label" sortOrder="5" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Customer EAV Attributes</label>
                    <source_model>Yireo\GoogleTagManager2\Config\Source\CustomerAttributes</source_model>
                    <comment>Customer EAV attributes to show in datalayer</comment>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="user_id_mode" type="select" translate="label comment" sortOrder="6" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>GA4 user_id mode</label>
                    <source_model>Yireo\GoogleTagManager2\Config\Source\UserIdMode</source_model>
                    <comment><![CDATA[None by default. <b>Email hash</b> emits HMAC-SHA256(normalized email) for logged-in customers, guest quotes and orders, so a guest order and a later account with the same email share the same GA4 user_id. <b>Customer ID</b> emits the Magento customer ID for logged-in customers only; guest orders remain anonymous. Email addresses are never emitted. Enabling this requires a privacy-policy and consent review; rotating the Magento crypt key changes all hashes.]]></comment>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="view_cart_occurances" type="select" translate="label" sortOrder="14" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>view_cart occurances</label>
                    <source_model>Yireo\GoogleTagManager2\Config\Source\ViewCartOccurancesOptions</source_model>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                    <comment>Where to generate the view_cart event</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="view_cart_on_mini_cart_expand_only" type="select" translate="label" sortOrder="15" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>view_cart only with expanded minicart</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="view_cart_occurances">everywhere</field>
                    </depends>
                    <comment>Generate the view_cart event only when expanding the minicart</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="serverside_enabled" type="select" translate="label" sortOrder="30" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Custom GTM container URL</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <comment>Load the GTM container from a custom URL (for instance a server-side GTM container) and only trigger the browser purchase event for the configured order states. This does not send any data server-to-server: for that, use the group "Server-Side Tracking" instead.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="serverside_gtm_url" type="text" translate="label" sortOrder="31" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Container URL</label>
                    <comment><![CDATA[<span>When a value is present in this field, data will send to this url instead of https://www.googletagmanager.com.
                    Default output: https://gtm-test123.uc.r.appspot.com. Create a cname in the dns records for a name like marketing.shopname.com</span><br/>
                    <b>Keep in mind</b>; enter a full url (with https://). ]]></comment>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="serverside_enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="order_states_for_purchase_event" type="multiselect" translate="label" sortOrder="32" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Orders states for purchase event</label>
                    <source_model>Yireo\GoogleTagManager2\Config\Source\OrderStateOptions</source_model>
                    <comment>Order states at which to trigger the purchase event. This is used by the setting "Custom GTM container URL" and by the server-side purchase trigger "When the order reaches one of the configured order states". When neither is used, the purchase event is triggered at any state.</comment>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="use_base_currency" type="select" translate="label" sortOrder="33" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Send Quote and Purchase data in base currency</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <comment>If enabled, purchase data will be sent in base currency. If disabled, purchase data will be sent in store currency.</comment>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="max_transaction_value" translate="label" sortOrder="33" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Maximum Transaction Value</label>
                    <comment>Maximum transaction value for purchase events. When an order value exceeds this amount, the transaction_value_adjusted field will be capped at this value. Leave empty or 0 to disable.</comment>
                    <validate>validate-number validate-zero-or-greater</validate>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="include_shipping_in_adjusted_value" type="select" translate="label" sortOrder="34" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Include Shipping in Adjusted Total</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <comment>If enabled, shipping costs will be included in the adjusted transaction value calculation. This setting works in conjunction with the Maximum Transaction Value setting.</comment>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
            </group>
            <group id="serverside_tracking" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="2" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                <label>Server-Side Tracking</label>
                <field id="enabled" type="select" translate="label comment" sortOrder="1" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Enabled</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <comment>Send ecommerce events server-to-server using the GA4 Measurement Protocol</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="destination" type="select" translate="label" sortOrder="2" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Destination</label>
                    <source_model>Yireo\GoogleTagManager2\ServerSide\Config\Source\Destination</source_model>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="sgtm_url" type="text" translate="label comment" sortOrder="3" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Server-side GTM URL</label>
                    <comment>Full HTTPS URL of your server-side GTM container (for instance https://sgtm.example.com). Events are sent to this URL plus /mp/collect.</comment>
                    <backend_model>Yireo\GoogleTagManager2\Config\Backend\SgtmUrl</backend_model>
                    <validate>validate-url</validate>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                        <field id="destination">sgtm</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="measurement_id" type="text" translate="label comment" sortOrder="4" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Measurement ID</label>
                    <comment>GA4 Measurement ID, starting with "G-"</comment>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="api_secret" type="obscure" translate="label comment" sortOrder="5" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>API secret</label>
                    <comment>Measurement Protocol API secret (GA4 Admin, Data Streams, Measurement Protocol API secrets)</comment>
                    <backend_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Backend\Encrypted</backend_model>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="events" type="multiselect" translate="label" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Events</label>
                    <source_model>Yireo\GoogleTagManager2\ServerSide\Config\Source\Events</source_model>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="purchase_trigger" type="select" translate="label comment" sortOrder="11" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Purchase trigger</label>
                    <source_model>Yireo\GoogleTagManager2\ServerSide\Config\Source\PurchaseTrigger</source_model>
                    <comment>The order states are configured with the setting "Orders states for purchase event"</comment>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="suppress_browser_purchase" type="select" translate="label comment" sortOrder="12" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Suppress browser purchase event</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <comment>Do not push the purchase event in the browser, when the purchase event is sent server-side</comment>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="dispatch_mode" type="select" translate="label comment" sortOrder="20" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Dispatch mode</label>
                    <source_model>Yireo\GoogleTagManager2\ServerSide\Config\Source\DispatchMode</source_model>
                    <comment>Cron sends pending events every minute. Message queue requires the consumer yireo_gtm2.serverside.event to run.</comment>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="require_consent" type="select" translate="label comment" sortOrder="21" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Require analytics consent</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <comment>Only applies when the consent banner of this extension is enabled</comment>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="send_user_id" type="select" translate="label comment" sortOrder="13" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Send customer ID as user_id</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <comment>Send the Magento customer ID of logged-in customers as user_id. Only enable this when your privacy policy allows it.</comment>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="validation_mode" type="select" translate="label comment" sortOrder="22" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Validation mode</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <comment>Send events to the validation endpoint (/debug/mp/collect) instead. Events are not recorded by GA4.</comment>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="max_attempts" type="text" translate="label" sortOrder="23" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Maximum attempts</label>
                    <validate>validate-digits validate-greater-than-zero</validate>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="retention_days" type="text" translate="label" sortOrder="24" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="0" showInStore="0">
                    <label>Retention of sent events (days)</label>
                    <validate>validate-digits validate-greater-than-zero</validate>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
            </group>
            <group id="consent" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="1" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                <label>Consent</label>
                <field id="enabled" type="select" translate="label" sortOrder="1" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Enabled</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                </field>
                <field id="privacy_statement_url" type="text" translate="label" sortOrder="3" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Privacy statement URL</label>
                    <comment>For example '/privacy-statement'</comment>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
            </group>
            <group id="giztop_bridge" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="10" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                <label>GIZTOP Theme Bridge (infinite scroll, quickview, layered navigation)</label>
                <comment><![CDATA[DOM bridge that re-emits <code>view_item_list</code> after AJAX list updates (Olegnax InfiniteScroll, Olegnax LayeredNavigation) and emits <code>add_to_cart</code> for Quickview submissions. All selectors default to the Luma theme markup and can be overridden per theme (for instance Olegnax Athlete2).]]></comment>
                <field id="enabled" type="select" translate="label" sortOrder="1" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Enabled</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                </field>
                <field id="product_selector" type="text" translate="label" sortOrder="2" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Product ID selector</label>
                    <comment><![CDATA[Selector used inside a product item to resolve the product entity ID (fallback when the item has no <code>data-entity-id</code> attribute).]]></comment>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="grid_selector" type="text" translate="label" sortOrder="3" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Product grid selector</label>
                    <comment>Comma-separated list of selectors matching the product grid/list containers that receive AJAX-appended items (infinite scroll).</comment>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="item_selector" type="text" translate="label" sortOrder="4" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Product item selector</label>
                    <comment>Selector matching a single product item (tile) within the grid.</comment>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="column_selector" type="text" translate="label" sortOrder="5" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Main column selector</label>
                    <comment>Selector of the container whose content is replaced by AJAX layered navigation. Observed with a MutationObserver.</comment>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="quickview_event" type="text" translate="label" sortOrder="6" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Quickview add-to-cart event</label>
                    <comment><![CDATA[Name of the jQuery event triggered on the parent document when the Quickview iframe submits its product form (Olegnax Quickview: <code>ajax:addToCart</code>).]]></comment>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="quickview_add_to_cart" type="select" translate="label" sortOrder="65" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Emit Quickview add_to_cart</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <comment><![CDATA[Disabled by default: the server-side <code>checkout_cart_add_product_complete</code> observer already emits the authoritative add_to_cart for Quickview submissions. Enable only if the server-side event is suppressed.]]></comment>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="debounce" type="text" translate="label" sortOrder="7" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Mutation debounce (ms)</label>
                    <validate>validate-digits validate-greater-than-zero</validate>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="dedupe_mode" type="select" translate="label" sortOrder="8" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>dataLayer dedupe mode</label>
                    <source_model>Yireo\GoogleTagManager2\Config\Source\BridgeDedupeMode</source_model>
                    <comment><![CDATA["Event" (default) dedupes identical-JSON payloads except transactional events (add_to_cart, remove_from_cart, purchase, refund); "All" dedupes every event (legacy); "None" disables dedupe. Per-event override via <code>meta.dedupe</code>.]]></comment>
                </field>
                <field id="debug" type="select" translate="label" sortOrder="9" showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Bridge debug logging</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
            </group>
        </section>
    </system>
</config>
